{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:08:29.107292Z","id":"eda8ec2e19b1080c8ded320310ae51a754e21fa469722ce700aa91f9c9b0f74a","body":{"detail":"Passed 5 of 5 alone. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"4b2e54f93bea887975ed8ca10f6ce06c75a80510dc194e3dea17d29c3ddf1db6"},"summary":"'the artifact deleted while the viewer types in it leaves the keyboard free' took 6.2 min in one gates run","supersedes":"5cfcbebcab703a3b4870ddeea008d1500403828dff957097ffddfc90ef323a60","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598645Z","id":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","body":{"detail":"The e2e specs check a tag by keyboard and click and close the editor with Escape. Nothing checks: a refused PATCH (too_many_tags past 20, or admin_only) showing its message and unchecking the box; a press outside or focus leaving closing the popover (ui/tag-editor.ts:45-55); the editor closing when the view ends or the viewer loses may_tag (tag-editor.ts:49). tag-picker.test.ts covers TagPicker with a stub onToggle only; TagEditor.svelte has no test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"1cd70e51a66a9bca34564e28e9aa3969833534b77b509e024240f2619cb50e33"},"suggested_fix":"Add a tags.spec.ts case that applies 20 tags by API and checks a 21st in the editor (alert text, box unchecked), and one that presses outside and tabs out; add a TagEditor unit test with a held PATCH.","summary":"No test covers the tag editor's refusal, the twenty-tag limit, or its popover closing paths","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.413479Z","id":"dd77e260972809c3b395e31ecb0c755883e70d48b51ed0a1ead805c6e6d04d1d","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts has five tests (lines 25, 109, 146, 164, 193); the editor case closes only with Escape (line 68). `grep -rln \"too_many_tags\\|TagEditor\\|tag-pop\" web/e2e web/shell/src` matches no test file (only .qual files, web/shell/src/artifact.ts and the components themselves). The untested close paths are web/shell/src/ui/tag-editor.ts:43 (pointerdown outside), :48 (state subscription on dispose / button disconnect) and :49-52 (focusout).","kind":"comment","references":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","summary":"confirmed: no test exercises the tag editor's refusal, the twenty-tag limit, or its outside-press/focus-out/view-end close paths","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.967090Z","id":"c868966943e5898b231bfbbb7193e8ce5b283b0c66a045c0c477666200cd54df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3113e2aed","summary":"Fixed: tags.spec.ts 'the tag editor shows a refusal past twenty tags…' checks a 21st tag's message and unchecked box and a press outside closing the editor; tag-editor.test.ts unit-tests TagEditor (order, refusal) and the popover closing on a press outside, focus leaving, Escape and the view ending or its button going (//web:unit passes; //web:e2e_rest tags.spec.ts inbox.spec.ts: 8 passed)","supersedes":"65c68033f882683e2c27e069e35b91b95cb96fb873d38681b225a40da114707b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:43:10.915052Z","id":"7382322766e2144d88b140e7fd8bfa7fd0b6a415bc25d1bfa8fa97a8deed1ac0","body":{"detail":"Under a machine load average of about 90 on 12 cores, `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest` with --grep for both tests and --repeat-each=10 passed all 60 runs (both modes, both key spacings). The failing run's output was not kept, so the failing assertion is unknown. Candidates: typeOn with spacing 0 queues every key while a Tab out of a cross-origin frame moves focus across processes, so a key routed to the frame before focus lands shifts the walk and the Space misses Send (the act-hint check at line 382); or the 5 s expect timeout on the pin or hint.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"ee819237803576b9feffc002d06c5e8f869fe405a08d7de2a4d3e31baa0c0fee"},"summary":"The subdomain variants of this test and of the one at line 405 failed under load in a gates run and were not reproduced","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/gesture.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:46:40.950981Z","id":"c60ce6267cbe1133e4b30f238fc1f0bf10b4d33a221cf36d60e3971716eb3051","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aff36e5dd","summary":"activationLapsed (web/e2e/time.ts) no longer gives up after 10 s, and the gesture project's timeout is 90 s. Evidence: bazelisk test //web:e2e_gesture --test_arg=e2e/gesture.spec.ts --test_arg=--grep=N14 --test_arg=--repeat-each=10 passed 120 of 120 at a load average of about 90 on 12 cores (slowest 12.3 s).","supersedes":"2c771fe38d3d0645ca5e87c1cabe0466ddc9ecbf9298c9257e4b5441eabf38d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/owner.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.756260Z","id":"343d7934ee148e517bc244dd7069f0374c70cf11abbb1da783a185519ea9142a","body":{"detail":"Failure: GitHub CI run 39440289806 (Linux, //web:e2e_rest, 8 workers): after setName(chrome, \"Alex\") and the safari field showing Alex, the LAN viewer's People and agents dialog had 0 .prow rows containing Alex (13 polls over 5000 ms). The other runs passed. The CI log has no trace or page state, so it does not show whether the rename event never reached the LAN viewer's page or reached it late; not investigated further.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"4528bdb052fc8e3b696fadd18fb236e3bfde096ccc35206b01c517bce162e7e4"},"summary":"The LAN viewer's roster did not show the owner's new name within 5 s once in CI","tags":["tests","flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:59:23.786760Z","id":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","body":{"detail":"Under load the LAN viewer's click on Add sometimes adds nothing: the daemon holds only 'Seeded one', the page still shows 'add invalid_argument' from the refusal before naming, and the title field still holds 'From the LAN'. That is either a click that never reached the form or an add refused again. Ruled out: the viewer's level is computed per request (crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs base_caller); the db capability does not narrow it; the rename does not reload the capability host. The pointer-reach change in web/e2e/fixtures.ts (6da3a3c9d) did not stop it (1 failure in 3 full-suite runs). Next: log the frame's submit/pointerdown events beside the /docs requests and their statuses. Re-enable once fixed; it covers a LAN viewer's write level.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"c32515fd370ab8de40ccf3b4c8e748f38c2a789a3c4d4274ff7df9c912cbbef8"},"summary":"LAN tracker test skipped (test.fixme) while it flakes under load","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:59:23.996246Z","id":"4801a7663df4428f43434a51ec0ffc73b4dff4db3ff7007a03a28a8b3290b455","body":{"detail":"The test presses Tab 12 times from the pin and expects Send focused. With all chrome mounted there are 13 stops (12 Tabs after the pin); on a loaded machine one lazily mounted control can arrive late, so the presses stop short. The sibling test near line 368 types a fixed 13-Tab sequence and depends on the same count. A fix that waited for the 13 stops before clicking into the page passed 4/4 targeted and 6/6 full-suite runs but was not proven at 10 repeats. Fix: wait for the chrome that adds stops, or Tab until Send has focus with a bound; then drop the test.fixme.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":421},"content_hash":"b8175a55701a13ed8ca1dd5946e39e4e0473f6c4702ea2ffd30104b625f71359"},"summary":"Keyboard-send test skipped in subdomain mode while a fixed Tab count misses Send","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T13:56:24.726868Z","id":"82d6b844288f0c587e481099243e594252588addea38aabd496d3d94fa18b172","body":{"detail":"Failure: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest under heavy machine load (the run of just test-affected main at 647958f22844's parent took 1.1 h for e2e_rest, with clax-server integration__1 to __3 timing out beside it). 'a daemon restart shows the notice in every tab, which reconnect with backoff and catch up' failed in the freshDaemon fixture (web/e2e/fixtures.ts:46, startDaemon: 'daemon did not become healthy (no stderr)'): daemon.json was written but /healthz did not answer before the deadline. The same target run alone at the same web code passed (539 passed, 1.5 min). Not seen in code the Clax app uses: the restart notice is the browser shell's stream reconnect.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":392},"end":{"line":420},"content_hash":"4c263d63c610b8197a0706c0b665765f930683207f621a2bb45bb87a4c317419"},"summary":"Under load, the restart test's fresh daemon fixture can miss its healthz deadline","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:44.888752Z","id":"ed55a45fe5e5a8358f7569ff3451473a26e06b44ded33964759dc6e4f76b3147","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:06f59eb43","summary":"Fixed in 06f59eb43: the late stop is the New comment box (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte imports NewComment.svelte apart). Holding its chunk (page.route on NewComment-*.js) put Send 11 stops from the pin and twelve Tabs passed it, in both modes. The test now waits until tabsFromPin(Send) is 12 (web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts:354) and runs in subdomain mode again. Beside 36 busy loops: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=60 --test_arg=--grep for this test, the other keyboard tests, attention.spec.ts and owner.spec.ts: 720 passed, 0 failed (60 per test and mode).","supersedes":"4801a7663df4428f43434a51ec0ffc73b4dff4db3ff7007a03a28a8b3290b455","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/owner.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:45.273941Z","id":"a5c66ac4d1b4885f3e0afc5bd5773201046f4244f1390762257619dd910ecfd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:90b8221e4","summary":"Fixed in 90b8221e4. Cause: a presence answer replaced the view's list even when a presence event had arrived since its request started. The LAN viewer's refetch on its stream's reconnect (after it names itself Mia) could be answered after the owner's rename event, putting the owner back unnamed: an e2e experiment holding that GET /api/artifacts/<id>/presence until the rename showed in the LAN roster, then delivering it, removed the Alex row in 3 of 3 runs before the fix and kept it in 5 of 5 after. web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.test.ts 'a presence answer to a request made before a presence event ...' fails without the ticket check ('expected 0 to be greater than 0') and passes with it. owner.spec.ts beside 36 busy loops: 120 of 120 passed (two --repeat-each=60 runs).","supersedes":"343d7934ee148e517bc244dd7069f0374c70cf11abbb1da783a185519ea9142a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:45.800375Z","id":"ef7f7ab7207af6acec1606e750bd6dcfaadc18366a6207ec9d9360dd3462e41e","body":{"detail":"Under a machine load average of about 90 on 12 cores, `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest` with --grep for both tests and --repeat-each=10 passed all 60 runs (both modes, both key spacings). The failing run's output was not kept, so the failing assertion is unknown. Candidates: typeOn with spacing 0 queues every key while a Tab out of a cross-origin frame moves focus across processes, so a key routed to the frame before focus lands shifts the walk and the Space misses Send (the act-hint check); or a Tab stop that mounts late. The second is now ruled out for this test: the New comment box loads in its own chunk, and with that chunk held Send is 11 stops from the pin, so this walk's Space misses Send; since 06f59eb43 the test waits for 12 stops first. After that, beside 36 busy loops, --repeat-each=60 twice passed 120 of 120 per mode for this test and for the line-418 test in both spacings. Close once a gates run passes them, or record the failing assertion if one recurs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"79786f2aa44348beaff726a8eeb1776a265d703c1a5433aedfe50e7aebfc32c7"},"summary":"The subdomain variants of this test and of the one at line 418 failed under load in a gates run and were not reproduced","supersedes":"7382322766e2144d88b140e7fd8bfa7fd0b6a415bc25d1bfa8fa97a8deed1ac0","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:46.444968Z","id":"8e2c7500ab49106afb7a0468cf750bbf2217562cbbf628c2c01414fdc6e7d0b1","body":{"detail":"Passed 5 of 5 alone. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":458},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"4b2e54f93bea887975ed8ca10f6ce06c75a80510dc194e3dea17d29c3ddf1db6"},"summary":"'the artifact deleted while the viewer types in it leaves the keyboard free' took 6.2 min in one gates run","supersedes":"eda8ec2e19b1080c8ded320310ae51a754e21fa469722ce700aa91f9c9b0f74a","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:59:47.015933Z","id":"dcffad35308977976745de57d02dbe41fdd9568788927ceaf22733b8186a6e8f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","summary":"Not reproduced, so still skipped. Unskipped, it passed 200 of 200 runs beside 36 busy loops (bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=200 --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='LAN: the tracker') and 3 of 3 in one run of the whole rest project with --repeat-each=3 beside 12 busy loops. One reading of the failure narrows it: before naming, the test's #save-note click set the status to 'note invalid_argument', so a status of 'add invalid_argument' after naming means the post-naming Add was submitted and refused again, not lost to a shield band or a missed click. Look next at which viewer that PUT /api/artifacts/<id>/docs/tasks/<id> carried and the level base_caller (crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs:72) gave it; a trace of a passing run shows one viewer cookie throughout and the add answered 200 right after the name's PUT. Two other flakes found here were orderings the test did not wait for (records 343d7934 and 4801a766).","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/boot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:26:43.829004Z","id":"4400a17aefd86816904abb3ac0f06db3f3839d35fcbb8bf1852c0f8032c0f6ba","body":{"detail":"Sandbox mode now frames http://<id>.localhost:<port>/_clax/v/<n>/ with the sandbox attribute (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs local_site; ArtifactController.site in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts), so the framed page has an opaque origin; a page it frames carries `frame-ancestors 'self' http://localhost:<port> http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs content_policy), which no opaque ancestor matches, and Chromium refuses it. Before site hosts, sandboxed content came from /c/ on the main origin with no frame-ancestors. Sandbox mode on loopback is reached only when the subdomain probe fails or a test forces it; Task 5 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md removes the probe and sandbox mode, and with it this fixme.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"707c3f30b18d8a1bbbbebe17a4587b97083df6301eb0d946c82c5df0355c1883"},"summary":"In sandbox mode a site page cannot frame the artifact's own pages: test.fixme for the sandbox variant","tags":["site-origins","e2e","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/boot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.335894Z","id":"54dd1b1025fc904203b8472f5fcaaa8a79726274b3df3b2da88946844bfb6e9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86ec4f43","summary":"Sandbox mode is gone, and with it the fixme: 'the shell frames the content on its site origin, and the artifact's pages frame each other' (web/e2e/boot.spec.ts) runs unsandboxed and passes in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest (boot.spec.ts, 4 of 4 runs with --repeat-each=4) at 86ec4f43.","supersedes":"4400a17aefd86816904abb3ac0f06db3f3839d35fcbb8bf1852c0f8032c0f6ba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373451Z","id":"99465763f2f3a99bf1250fe75fdf6b6e1249076a12680694a12cc4da3e0e10f7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","summary":"Proposed close (obsolete) for the owner: 86ec4f43 removes LAN viewers from a local daemon, and with them the skipped 'LAN: the tracker…' test in web/e2e/contract.spec.ts.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/artifact.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373609Z","id":"ae9dbb58f8ad38816070c284122091064ead3bb8ec1e95972d5cd57b0cd65f3e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"96c0f3dc1012f373cc2987fbfe7fef90f4ed47c2dd7159c8a36f680c6a8d6428","summary":"Proposed close (obsolete) for the owner: 86ec4f43 removes sandbox mode, so web/e2e/artifact.spec.ts has no sandbox run of the vote tests any more; the one run passes 4 of 4 with --repeat-each=4.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/site-runtime.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.382911Z","id":"f84639a709d4bd94f8e60c3c4d4afd4d5ba11988e4fc4464b7183088c6c34398","body":{"detail":"'a private site framed in the shell reads its db through its own origin' is test.fixme: a local shell's frame never arrives on this base (record c0919532 on crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs), and the framed specs of web/e2e (db.spec.ts, room.spec.ts, capabilities.spec.ts) fail the same way. What runs is web/bridge/test/origin.test.ts, origin-client.test.ts, room-socket.test.ts and web/shell/src/caps/{db,room}.test.ts. The merge that makes the shell frame each site through a site code (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Tasks 5 and 6) enables this spec and the framed ones, and they gate that merge.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"a30cb7d8c9da284433d79fda6e58ca6b8f99c00875fb242fb8994fe10199b54d"},"summary":"The framed page runtime (a frame's db, room and user through its own origin, the shell's db and room reports) is covered by unit tests alone","tags":["site-origins","testing","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/site-runtime.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:34:07.317771Z","id":"cc5624ee17c8e07441b05e1b5f876e0f5e1762e9a568df9a582f744eefc85a77","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:754dadb3","summary":"Fixed: the framed spec runs. `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--retries=0 --test_arg=site-runtime.spec.ts --test_arg=room.spec.ts` passes 'a private site framed in the shell reads its db through its own origin' (its frame's runtime calls go to <id>.localhost/_clax/api/docs and none to the public origin's /api/), and room.spec.ts's framed specs and its hosted guest spec pass.","supersedes":"f84639a709d4bd94f8e60c3c4d4afd4d5ba11988e4fc4464b7183088c6c34398","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/claxbot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.221428Z","id":"a8b5c77c9dd50794e19ae803007fdab836b13b8f897b76151cebebd7c99e71dc","body":{"detail":"Until the server side lands, stubBot answers /api/me/bot, /api/bot/*, /api/admin/*, /api/settings and /api/audit at the network layer. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 12 asks for these tests against a daemon with a scripted model provider; once it serves the routes, the stubs should go and the runs come from a fake Messages API.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"5f45780a1c1c74345040c23bd6804ee1767fb09e0ec29966708376983012c02c"},"summary":"ClaxBot's browser tests answer its API with route stubs, not a daemon running ClaxBot","tags":["claxbot","revisit:the daemon serves ClaxBot's routes","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/claxbot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.357446Z","id":"73c2198e24921acdfe002581f7b97306e86f888ab340d162fd0bd5b614c685a3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a8b5c77c9dd50794e19ae803007fdab836b13b8f897b76151cebebd7c99e71dc","summary":"Settings no longer has a stub: 'Settings reads the daemon's own settings route…' in web/e2e/claxbot.spec.ts reads and writes the daemon's GET/PUT /api/settings; the other ClaxBot routes are still stubbed.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/claxbot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:44.513789Z","id":"d02c36964aff1994065cfa4d66f1c58611a4f36dcd1ccd7d0e363f96530ba91d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a8b5c77c9dd50794e19ae803007fdab836b13b8f897b76151cebebd7c99e71dc","summary":"Partly addressed: web/e2e/claxbot-daemon.spec.ts runs a Send to ClaxBot on a daemon with a scripted Messages API (web/e2e/fake-messages.ts) through the run panel to its end, the audit view, and the admin people, provider and pricing pages, nothing stubbed (git:d99deaf8; bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest with --grep passes); the stubbed Send and admin-people tests are gone. Still stubbed in claxbot.spec.ts: the New tile's build (the run it replays), the at-limit week, and the You and audit pages at phone width. The reply the run posts is not checked until the server's BotHost writes land.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/claxbot.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:37:23.693992Z","id":"34a0430fbe84066cea3e863f8d77285f80807bea52d195bdc9caa1aff40cc9a2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d02c36964aff1994065cfa4d66f1c58611a4f36dcd1ccd7d0e363f96530ba91d","summary":"Since git:61ec9bfb the daemon-backed Send test also checks that the run's finish summary lands on the thread as ClaxBot's reply (web/e2e/claxbot-daemon.spec.ts; bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest with --grep passes).","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/subpages.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:22.638213Z","id":"f9192196eb4d98a38eb3fece2da9f4dd045a458765727602d104e6fe50ffad06","body":{"detail":"Passed 10 of 10 alone. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"a3cf97db0c4aa916e575080620ad46a5fdea32488ae9753d41958c844b9c8121"},"summary":"'one link inside the frame is one history entry' fails about 1 run in 120 under load","supersedes":"99e106564689907ff0dd6bc26b4241f7beaf7f48a38ba39c37d598e83e89fc8c","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/subpages.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:23.217079Z","id":"cb348dffcca6e435436777ffda4ee69871e576b57899e64f515c7dbacb02d986","body":{"detail":"Seen 2026-10-05 at load 20 to 35; passed on rerun. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"6c8ff9383285acce94ced1a9f63fcdd20d9ea2639d2e77a579bf79daa036ec9f"},"summary":"The fragment test's page URL check flakes under load","supersedes":"3892dd574863e73cd63111b360ac40fe885eed924f1ddba6cef666c696d6b635","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/changelog.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:23.953778Z","id":"cc5c4fd1f4cafa89c15bad512a5ae19171bc955c632ec3deea7cda113110fd95","body":{"detail":"Seen 2026-10-05 at load 20 to 35 at line 43; passed on rerun. Not yet diagnosed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"b1479ec5a0387ee0b140b3c6053997b5d53754d9f084adfc3c929693955e32fe"},"summary":".thread-pin.addressed not found within 5 s under load","supersedes":"1fb89fe2180e9ab019630a1a78c0b9f76ee918b2667200528bf8b5c7849a2206","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/artifact.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:24.593062Z","id":"b5fe308c4570ab96b06de95e1003af084e53dafbc83d735ada90cdb157ea5d68","body":{"detail":"Failure: in one run of just ci, //web:e2e_rest failed on 'sandbox: a second viewer's vote 2 s after another viewer's vote reloaded it publishes' with Error: globalThis.claxTestClock.advance(2000): TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'advance'). Rerun alone (bazel test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=...) both modes passed, and the whole e2e_rest lane alone passed (347 passed, 53 skipped). The clock was advanced in a page that had not, or no longer, loaded the test build's hook, perhaps across the reload the test makes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"01532a45d96bb017db4a7955069d63d3bdaa4d656bcc4ffdd54c3a998fa54616"},"summary":"The sandbox run of \"a second viewer's vote 2 s after another viewer's vote reloaded it publishes\" failed once in just ci: the page had no test clock","supersedes":"96c0f3dc1012f373cc2987fbfe7fef90f4ed47c2dd7159c8a36f680c6a8d6428","tags":["tests","flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/echo-chrome.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:25.641956Z","id":"e22e8536325cc411d15a1935aa24c0b46308a0753d89420caa7234e3b2402407","body":{"detail":"Under a machine load average of about 90 on 12 cores, `bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest` with --grep for both tests and --repeat-each=10 passed all 60 runs (both modes, both key spacings). The failing run's output was not kept, so the failing assertion is unknown. Candidates: typeOn with spacing 0 queues every key while a Tab out of a cross-origin frame moves focus across processes, so a key routed to the frame before focus lands shifts the walk and the Space misses Send (the act-hint check); or a Tab stop that mounts late. The second is now ruled out for this test: the New comment box loads in its own chunk, and with that chunk held Send is 11 stops from the pin, so this walk's Space misses Send; since 06f59eb43 the test waits for 12 stops first. After that, beside 36 busy loops, --repeat-each=60 twice passed 120 of 120 per mode for this test and for the line-418 test in both spacings. Close once a gates run passes them, or record the failing assertion if one recurs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"ad346628313f0a95a445e9e10d5797233f331a3d824f5266409c2c01b507d43d"},"summary":"The subdomain variants of this test and of the one at line 418 failed under load in a gates run and were not reproduced","supersedes":"ef7f7ab7207af6acec1606e750bd6dcfaadc18366a6207ec9d9360dd3462e41e","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/contract.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.529558Z","id":"712bc04cfa33748f4b8f7ee3ef68ac05ec7f3bd989ba68c26ffde784a950b02d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9151ba2de305d4a97a4fb5e72a2b2c8b82b6ec791e336aacdf621260fa8a325e","summary":"The skipped LAN tracker test is gone from web/e2e/contract.spec.ts with LAN viewing itself (commit 86ec4f43 removed LAN viewing; the merge ca09c4f7 keeps it removed). Proposed close: obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T22:22:36.962987Z","id":"fdf0b2fe4c59e36f3a47fe1dece971b2af6610c7757fb0082c4c32a1bf243685","body":{"detail":"In three full runs of //web:e2e_rest under just check (logs target/merge-logs/check.log, check2.log, check3.log) the expectation that a phone's view of the artifact shows no '.topbar .tedit' found one; the same test passed alone three times (--grep=tags --repeat-each=3) and in a 79-test subset. Not yet known whether main fails it under the same load, or whether the site-origin view differs while the phone's new context resolves its viewer.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"653a7fcd4b380baa8be7652708aea84384cc638020ce81a57223f25e19d1b6da"},"summary":"The phone half of the twenty-tags test fails in the whole rest suite and passes alone","tags":["e2e","flaky","site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/tags.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:15:04.998596Z","id":"aa9c5d72cdb16e8261273fb55b3cdccf3f3cae72a08315f81945ebec20107882","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6451a18c","summary":"The branch's fault, fixed in 6451a18c. On main (9bb62110) the full //web:e2e_rest passes, 548 passed, tags.spec.ts:170 included; there the phone is a LAN viewer. Since 86ec4f43 removed LAN viewing the phone opens the page on loopback, where it is the owner, who may tag, so '.topbar .tedit' count 0 held only until its shell had its token. The test now expects the owner's edit button. Evidence: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--repeat-each=3 --test_arg=tags.spec.ts passes (15 passed, 3 skipped), and the full //web:e2e_rest passes, 424 passed.","supersedes":"fdf0b2fe4c59e36f3a47fe1dece971b2af6610c7757fb0082c4c32a1bf243685","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:33.059038Z","id":"bb48f5a38e7cbae6a82984a0ac4ab2860d5e58e042c9411c328a4d2c1b55eef5","body":{"detail":"//web:e2e_rest fails on every push to main since 647958f22 (run 40116028683 on f57ec462b among them). The five tests fail the same way against mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble's Chromium through PW_TEST_CONNECT_WS_ENDPOINT, and pass 11/11 on macOS Chromium. Traces show Linux headless-shell keeps a mouse at (0,0) that Chromium hit-tests again after layout changes: (a) after a touch tap in the frame, a mouseover of header.topbar at (0,0) (firesTouchEvents false) reaches notePointerOver (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:302-310), which sets pointerOnFrameSince = -1 before the deferred blur check enters the frame, so entryByViewer is false and the pick is refused; (b) in app mode (no top bar) a mouseover of iframe.frame at page load, before any shell input, counts as the pointer's arrival, so a pick no viewer attested is taken. With channel 'chromium' (new headless) the (0,0) events go, but the touch's mouseover of the iframe does not reach the shell either, and the pick is still refused. The shell's rules and the tests are unchanged; record 8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2 (web/bridge/src/long-press.ts) already notes long-press is unverified outside desktop Chromium.\n\nOptions: (1) skip these five tests on Linux, keeping them on macOS runs only; (2) tell touch arrivals from mouse boundary events in gesture.ts (ignore mouseover with sourceCapabilities.firesTouchEvents false that the browser synthesises without movement), a change to what the shell counts as the viewer's gesture; (3) run CI's browser tests on a macOS runner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"7065e4d030fcdfb7af8b39aa1a18a38d5aee65b398ad5203f8e328c0708f352d"},"summary":"The touch-pick e2e tests fail on Linux Chromium, CI's browser: hold-drag.spec.ts:78, :106, :233 and long-press.spec.ts:43, :58 since 647958f22","tags":["status:needs-decision","ci","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:27.693129Z","id":"d4ef35ce1be4be29aaa8c1138c5a8593fc728bc528b4784cbc39b4be3809ed3d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9b0f37237","summary":"Fixed in the shell (option 2): web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts counts only real movement as arriving or leaving. Mouse boundary events at the latest pointer position with no movement, or from a vanished shell element before any pointer event, are ignored for arrival and departure, and so are mouse boundary events after a touch until a real mouse move. Against mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble, hold-drag.spec.ts:78, :106 and :257 (formerly :233) and long-press.spec.ts:46 and :61 (formerly :43 and :58) pass unchanged, 65/65 over --repeat-each=5. //web:e2e_gesture passes there too. The new tests long-press.spec.ts:77 and hold-drag.spec.ts:233 fail on macOS against the old gesture.ts and pass with it.","supersedes":"bb48f5a38e7cbae6a82984a0ac4ab2860d5e58e042c9411c328a4d2c1b55eef5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/working.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T23:36:43.683856Z","id":"0d88743c4686392868390bdf913b48d6f1c936c29d5501d8e1e8ce364a7137a4","body":{"detail":"gallery.locator(\".card-wrap\", { hasText: \"Working\" }) matches every card whose text contains Working (e.g. an artifact titled \"App send no frames session\" showing \"Clax working on 1\"), so when another spec in the same e2e daemon leaves such an artifact, strict mode fails with \"resolved to 2 elements\" (seen under //web:e2e_rest on the quickstart branches, passing again alone). Find the card by this test's artifact ID instead, e.g. its data attribute or href /a/<id>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"8f9029c3bb272dd663a43d4e9086f5aeb09ec7d0f1f9d3ecf0da9032896d59f5"},"summary":"The gallery card is found by the text \"Working\", which other tests' artifacts also match","tags":["flaky","test","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/shell-capability.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:24:04.674637Z","id":"ddc3da6d09ed3d0b79415db8ceeb3e2a296ca1b74525d89c0132ca02b9a66b68","body":{"detail":"`the_ring_follows_a_scrolling_container_and_goes_when_its_control_leaves_it` posts 25 threads so the sidebar overflows, and clicks Threads only `if` `aside.sidebar` is hidden (line 177). That hides an assumption about which viewport and layout opens the sidebar by default: a layout change that always or never shows it passes through the branch without telling the test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"80bdd03d394db3aa045f2f76cd6441abedf806f4509e53d2ac6557556b9f8713"},"summary":"The scroll test hand-builds 25 threads and branches on whether the sidebar is visible","tags":["revisit:the sidebar's default visibility or the Threads button's place changes","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/working.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:52:38.801083Z","id":"d7a15559ad3b7ee36255d427d10b807c8f8d1fec4f9d6729ee4949b7ff2d4416","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:65a38967","summary":"Fixed in 65a38967: the gallery card is found by its a.card[href=\"/a/<artifact ID>\"] link. //web:e2e_rest, in the full just test-affected quickstart run on branch quickstart-g with this commit as base (433 specs, other artifacts' 'Working' cards present), passed working.spec.ts:32, which had failed there before the fix.","supersedes":"0d88743c4686392868390bdf913b48d6f1c936c29d5501d8e1e8ce364a7137a4","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/permissions.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T04:07:03.129900Z","id":"7eb1c3fd064d611b639dca7f3f8fb618fa177eee259554f0ad8fc18b0b6f2939","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/permissions.spec.ts covers the local daemon only: the owner sees the bar and a connected person does not. On a hosted daemon the daemon says may_approve for the page's maker (crates/clax-server/src/routes/permissions.rs may_approve), so a member who publishes a page sees the bar and approves without net or sample grants. Only the controller's use of may_approve is unit-tested (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.test.ts, shows_the_bar_only_when_the_daemon_says_the_viewer_may_approve).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"22c667e9cefafd1498c3a07c76a1217ae8bf50195f2e5a47315f881654bd416b"},"summary":"No browser test covers a hosted member seeing the approval bar on their own page","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/shell-capability.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:07:49.379162Z","id":"a77b96f244b8e872efd4333ff41caff5d4266a439fc7e28a40fae43fe0d0d06c","body":{"detail":"`the_ring_follows_a_scrolling_container_and_goes_when_its_control_leaves_it` posts 25 threads so the sidebar overflows, and clicks Threads only `if` `aside.sidebar` is hidden (line 177). That hides an assumption about which viewport and layout opens the sidebar by default: a layout change that always or never shows it passes through the branch without telling the test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"d81659953156a39c1ff7981b5b7b81538c6200ae401edab6982e8db2062033e9"},"summary":"The scroll test hand-builds 25 threads and branches on whether the sidebar is visible","supersedes":"ddc3da6d09ed3d0b79415db8ceeb3e2a296ca1b74525d89c0132ca02b9a66b68","tags":["revisit:the sidebar's default visibility or the Threads button's place changes","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:50.058842Z","id":"94c0bbf23c7cd3bb49a7fc5fcc48d2cca8d80bef636503e333e2ad4f4c3278c0","body":{"detail":"bazel test //web:e2e_chrome_overlay --test_arg='--grep=follow a hot reload' --test_arg=--repeat-each=15: 5 failed, 10 passed before; 15 passed after. A console log of the failing runs showed watcher changes to index.html, users/1.html and users/2.html (never edited by a test) right after the marker was set, then a navigation of the main frame.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:eede74ae2","summary":"Fixed: the live site's Vite server no longer watches its pages (server.watch.ignored **/*.html), so a late FSEvents report of the copy cannot fully reload the page","supersedes":"bdb345cbe43d326414c751adf197c87d0bf5ecfbafff8869d8d9464acab3e080","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
