{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:50.716250Z","id":"b5723b2a99c8f004e2ef694ebae66c4748cfbd2fb2a8dad7f730b18272ed977e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"82d6b844288f0c587e481099243e594252588addea38aabd496d3d94fa18b172","summary":"One way to miss the healthz deadline is fixed in 529ba9edc: localhost resolves to ::1 first, and a Bazel server listening on [::1] at the port the daemon got on 127.0.0.1 answered the health check; startDaemon now restarts on such a port. Seen once (streams.spec.ts:348, 'daemon did not become healthy (no stderr)'); unconfirmed as this record's cause.","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fork.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T14:50:50.716327Z","id":"bdacf4726f978aac3dec8026a545d715710ebf32f121d55443f5b5cf44836d5b","body":{"detail":"At 74d6b37ad, bazel test //web:e2e_rest --runs_per_test=4 failed one run at fork.spec.ts:41 (locator.click: waiting for '.topbar button[aria-label=More]', 30 s). The test passed 120 of 120 with --grep=Fork --repeat-each=30 alone and in 6 other full runs. The button needs viewReady and MoreMenu.svelte's lazy import (web/shell/src/ui/more-menu.svelte.ts:73), whose failure is swallowed; which one was missing is unknown. Failed runs now keep the page's error context and screenshot under bazel-testlogs/web/e2e_rest/test.outputs (f7d6f254a).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":46},"content_hash":"e18837e9e53d5fb8810833ea9766bcb4d3fa6d0724b5c245fbb11d4bd4dc699a"},"summary":"The phone-width Fork test once timed out waiting for the More button, in 1 of 7 full //web:e2e_rest runs","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:21:42.130454Z","id":"198a99293cadb4b40e8f04adff061e8fb71d8c5b2acc38163c55a464c58d4273","body":{"detail":"runMigration's limit (web/bridge/src/harness.ts:307-331) is measured with the page's real clock in this e2e, so line 153's totalMs: 3000 is a budget that loading migrate.js and the page's db must fit, and line 167's page.waitForTimeout(200) stands in for 'no more writes arrive'. Both conflict with AGENTS.md's rule against sleeps and wall-clock budgets. The timing rule itself is covered with injected timers in the bridge's unit tests; this e2e could inject a clock into the harness deps, or assert only what needs no time (the answer is the over-time error, and a reloaded view stops the writes, polled against a version read after reload).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"b8f78c452a6e57755429e3fdb00a3f475b025a6297d3febb9207b1ffa92f1b0c"},"summary":"The over-time migration test still runs on real time: a 3000 ms totalMs and a 200 ms sleep","tags":["session:claude-code:3e8d3518-726a-4423-93d1-4f827624829c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570301Z","id":"bd66b770972b22928a4704fee21f9618898e1e224b304723c8bf4d75cf9207b8","body":{"detail":"//web:e2e_chrome_overlay failed this test with `Error: timed out` in a full test-affected run and again run alone; a third run failed 'comment on a dev server page, reach the agent, and follow a hot reload' (line 169) instead. Neither touches code the hosted Worker's Bazel build changed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":695},"end":{"line":695},"content_hash":"8963b536cc7aafabecf2367e7f034d1cc7ca1d3444e22dbd994331d385a18601"},"summary":"'a native host slow to start' timed out (2.0 min) in two runs, once alone","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/sharing.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570339Z","id":"6ba4ad018b93b2ca7b22b513ff834e53696faf08c02efc34776d05051ae985e7","body":{"detail":"//web:e2e_rest failed this test in a full test-affected run and again run alone; a third run, alone, passed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":188},"content_hash":"badbb21fcddcc059b97d41cf6097e1c37553ded440b34f6424e77c1f50ef3e40"},"summary":"'comments switch refuses a guest comment' failed once alone: locator.selectOption: Test ended (30 s)","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:38:21.825222Z","id":"792477f7d7a24748d19e9ef95e355c2645b260403c2243b699022f5a00d7c5fe","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bd66b770972b22928a4704fee21f9618898e1e224b304723c8bf4d75cf9207b8","summary":"In a full `just ci` run //web:e2e_chrome_overlay failed 'comment on a dev server page, reach the agent, and follow a hot reload' (line 169, 3.8 min), and passed when rerun alone.","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/hosted-demo-worker.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T01:37:41.631055Z","id":"a4ae5dcec27344581a855273701c571e6c66737358e54ad1206bea01be708e4f","body":{"detail":"It runs only with CLAX_E2E_WORKER=1 (about 30 s on a warm build), so scripts/quality_gates.sh never runs it; adding it to lane_e2e after `worker e2e` would grow the e2e lane past the suite's two-minute budget. BUILT checks only that crates/clax-worker/build/index.js and web/dist/index.html exist: the Worker embeds web/dist when built (crates/clax-server/src/routes/shell.rs, rust-embed), so a Worker built before the last scripts/build-web.sh serves entry pages naming the previous chunks, and a shell change is not what the check sees. A check could compare build/index_bg.wasm's mtime with web/node_modules/.clax-web-built's.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 1a5cdcce (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347): line 115 changed when build.sh's output moved, and BUILT now checks target/clax-worker/build/index.js. Under Bazel, //crates/clax-worker:bundle depends on //web:dist, so a Bazel build of the Worker is not older than web/dist; the native build still can be.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"06a56dac32be6e37cdafe379d1806accdfb7a380147c104066470b2a5ddd891c"},"summary":"The Worker demo check is not in the quality gates, and a Worker built before web/dist passes its built check while serving the old shell","supersedes":"1a5cdcce390a1102487d142d40a3776fefaea7ef6529283576968f4568ad4367","tags":["demo","worker","tests","status:deferred","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:14:57.852890Z","id":"d39218df0a2ae6840c57466f0af8ebcd1dbddfbef3ea987d6ec8921299f0ef7b","body":{"detail":"On 2026-10-29 //web:e2e_rest failed once in a bazelisk test run alongside //crates/clax-server/..., //crates/clax-worker/... and the web checks (24 targets): app-mode.spec.ts:384, expect.poll(back).toBe(false), Expected false, Received true, 'Timeout 5000ms exceeded while waiting on the predicate', after the hash had returned to '' at line 383. The same lane run alone right after passed (58.9s). The change under test touched no app-mode code (the hosted landing page, crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs and crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs). A 5 s poll is a wall-clock budget, which AGENTS.md's load-tolerance rule asks tests not to have; the predicate the poll waits on may need a signal of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":385},"content_hash":"827103a3b7530b41961d0ec644bf371567eddfe4e7e1ec16b7e271bf3dd353f6"},"summary":"back()'s fragments-and-pages test fails under load: its last poll sees back() still true after 5 s","tags":["flaky","e2e","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/sharing.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T20:54:10.781331Z","id":"35fe5d07d55e08859659f03a21fa861f721ddf9e8f89624b1250da47fe40bb66","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b3b043bd","summary":"Fixed: the Share dialog dropped a General access change made while the Comments switch's reload was in flight (act() refuses while busy; web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte), so the link-access select never appeared. The selects are now disabled while busy and put back on refusal, and selectOption waits for them. Evidence: unit test 'takes no General access change while a Comments change is in flight' in web/shell/src/share.test.ts failed before the fix and passes after (bazelisk test //web:unit //web:typecheck //web:lint: 3 tests pass); bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep --test_arg='comments switch refuses a guest comment' --runs_per_test=20: PASSED, 20 of 20 runs '1 passed'; bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --runs_per_test=3: PASSED, each run 444 passed, 62 skipped.","supersedes":"6ba4ad018b93b2ca7b22b513ff834e53696faf08c02efc34776d05051ae985e7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.841111Z","id":"459208a976429bcb7100a9e33bd267e6b0ff0a0989e16f1b2d5c4032ff3d6a60","body":{"detail":"trustContext and trustBrowser give each browser context the worker's daemons' owner browser session cookies (localhost and 127.0.0.1), as every local browser was the owner's once the shell fetched /api/token; asLocalViewer opts a context out for viewer tests. The global fetch wrapper here sends a request with neither Authorization nor a cookie to a worker daemon as a viewer minted by the debug-build route POST /api/_test/viewers. A test that means to send no credential at all must set a cookie or Authorization header of its own, or call plainFetch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"3c96fca16705d8da50041f3f50cbd461d68037a9ad5332685eb390c3b000e695"},"summary":"The browser tests make every context the owner's browser and every credential-less Node fetch an unnamed local viewer","tags":["tests","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:22.539528Z","id":"5270e043bdb932b962530a300f6f6ff5974661b6184e1c25c94ec453b44cf72e","body":{"detail":"This test checks that a publish reaches all 14 interested tabs within expect's 5 s timeout and logs the latencies; its former 500 ms bound was removed because wall-clock budgets in functional tests fail under load. The time-to-usable perf gate (web/perf) measures a tab's first paint and comment readiness, and scripts/perf-clients.py measures delivery to raw /api/stream clients, so delivery through the shared-worker hub to tabs is judged by no machine-scaled budget.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"88bb3bff31f4a493c95de0da980670497784345a77df890009cf86b3b9389241"},"suggested_fix":"Add a publish-to-tab delivery measure to the time-to-usable perf gate, scaled by its control like its other measures.","summary":"No gate judges how fast a publish reaches open tabs","supersedes":"067e86b131a6604c662a4ddc88c5bbc8fb80134b3435996a6131e758c86fa1b9","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:22.635743Z","id":"faa8984a9f19dc2ae6d189d43c31fa1df5123c6fe80bc8c8271fe66201fd4034","body":{"detail":"Failure: bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest under heavy machine load (the run of just test-affected main at 647958f22844's parent took 1.1 h for e2e_rest, with clax-server integration__1 to __3 timing out beside it). 'a daemon restart shows the notice in every tab, which reconnect with backoff and catch up' failed in the freshDaemon fixture (web/e2e/fixtures.ts:46, startDaemon: 'daemon did not become healthy (no stderr)'): daemon.json was written but /healthz did not answer before the deadline. The same target run alone at the same web code passed (539 passed, 1.5 min). Not seen in code the Clax app uses: the restart notice is the browser shell's stream reconnect.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":397},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"4c263d63c610b8197a0706c0b665765f930683207f621a2bb45bb87a4c317419"},"summary":"Under load, the restart test's fresh daemon fixture can miss its healthz deadline","supersedes":"82d6b844288f0c587e481099243e594252588addea38aabd496d3d94fa18b172","tags":["flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:26:21.117885Z","id":"af3e0c42898b1314e99968a68dd4670138b9a3f42f776c21680add16b34f8cc9","body":{"detail":"startDaemon (web/e2e/fixtures.ts) waited a wall-clock 20 s for daemon.json and /healthz. It now waits until the daemon answers or exits (a daemon that exits fails with its stderr), bounded by the test's or fixture's timeout; opts.startMs still caps it for a caller that passes one (web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts). daemon.json is written immediately before axum::serve starts (crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs serve_core), so a missed health check after it is load; the [::1] trap of b5723b2a cannot catch a restart either, since a nonzero --port skips any port port_held finds held on 127.0.0.1 or ::1 (crates/clax-core/src/daemon.rs port_held, used by bind_first_free in crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs). 'a daemon restart shows the notice in every tab...' keeps test.setTimeout(30_000) for its two starts, a stop and the tabs' reconnect, so a run as loaded as the one recorded can still time it out; not reproducible here. bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest: 444 passed. Left open until it is seen again or the owner closes it.","kind":"comment","references":"faa8984a9f19dc2ae6d189d43c31fa1df5123c6fe80bc8c8271fe66201fd4034","summary":"The fixture's own 20 s deadline is gone (git:e34eaa8a4); the restart test's 30 s test timeout still bounds it under load","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T00:57:26.304401Z","id":"3118c02b741ff4d068bcb02429f92ac0d5b4c76d5bba057042621355ab0975c8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:272a19376","summary":"The restart test waits on no wall clock: the stream hub's reconnect wait runs on the shell's clock (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts RETRY_LABEL, via clock.ts after), the test checks the hub is waiting on it (hubsWaiting) and runs it at once in the shared worker (hubRetryNow), and every step waits with timeout 0; the 120 s test timeout only stops a hang. bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest passes (the test in 2.7 s alone; the whole project in 92 s), as does //web:e2e_chrome_overlay.","supersedes":"faa8984a9f19dc2ae6d189d43c31fa1df5123c6fe80bc8c8271fe66201fd4034","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/streams.spec.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T03:31:22.746075Z","id":"7424078c1df23744e0f35df8bebbfedc3b45ec89ca8f90260de57996ccd2f117","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3118c02b741ff4d068bcb02429f92ac0d5b4c76d5bba057042621355ab0975c8","summary":"Commit 272a19376 cited by this close was re-signed as 05edfe9a1 (same tree, author and message).","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588576Z","id":"43f0ab56a8aea53baf4368c4c98a24850114a4cabd75a76d8d458502faea437d","body":{"detail":"localBrowser (lines 41-51, cached per daemon), asLocalViewer (:177-183) and namedViewer (:613-619) each POST /api/_test/viewers with the token, check the answer differently (namedViewer does not check it at all) and build the clax_viewer cookie by hand.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"04eec65410256c71b46fe016238bc9c5005c6ab5d53618d0f46e60127c110e08"},"suggested_fix":"Add one `mintViewer(d: {base, token}): Promise<string>` returning the cookie value, with the ok check, and use it in all three (localBrowser keeps its per-daemon cache around it).","summary":"fixtures.ts mints a local viewer through /api/_test/viewers in three separate places","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","duplication","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.464858Z","id":"1ca766adcb96cdac9d67e0495fae77420ecd8f4359e9e7fa364a350a230dd484","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts:45 (localBrowser, checks r.ok), :180 (asLocalViewer, checks minted.ok) and :617 (namedViewer, no ok check before minted.json()) each POST /api/_test/viewers with the bearer token and build the clax_viewer cookie by hand.","kind":"comment","references":"43f0ab56a8aea53baf4368c4c98a24850114a4cabd75a76d8d458502faea437d","summary":"confirmed: three copies of the /api/_test/viewers mint","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:03:24.022763Z","id":"f615c19f752cd1ef679d54f2060b4d11e7863fe0a236c2f887a49c5dbbfcf9f2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4885a18e1","summary":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts mintViewer posts /api/_test/viewers with the ok check and returns the cookie value; localBrowser (cached), asLocalViewer and namedViewer use it. bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest passes.","supersedes":"43f0ab56a8aea53baf4368c4c98a24850114a4cabd75a76d8d458502faea437d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/e2e/fixtures.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:03:24.221713Z","id":"28742ce592670711d4b02f1bbb67e10ef4e7826680c7ce346369f20453abd0a0","body":{"detail":"trustContext and trustBrowser give each browser context the worker's daemons' owner browser session cookies (localhost and 127.0.0.1), as every local browser was the owner's once the shell fetched /api/token; asLocalViewer opts a context out for viewer tests. The global fetch wrapper here sends a request with neither Authorization nor a cookie to a worker daemon as a viewer minted by the debug-build route POST /api/_test/viewers. A test that means to send no credential at all must set a cookie or Authorization header of its own, or call plainFetch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"da7dcc439c5e5412c988769c7e97f0475d5c7a09e91bdab49be45559208a5728"},"summary":"The browser tests make every context the owner's browser and every credential-less Node fetch an unnamed local viewer","supersedes":"459208a976429bcb7100a9e33bd267e6b0ff0a0989e16f1b2d5c4032ff3d6a60","tags":["tests","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
